       "system": "http://hl7.org/fhir/sid/icd-10",
       "code": "K21.9"
      }
     ]
    },
    "note": [
     {
      "text": "52-year-old male presenting with burning in the chest and stomach after meals for 2 months. Character: burning sensation; radiation: up to the throat; aggravated by spicy and oily food; relieved by antacid. Severity 8/10. Associated: nausea, sour belching. PMH: Hypertension for 6 years; Coronary artery disease, stent 6 years ago. Drugs: Amlodipine 5 mg; Aspirin 75 mg; Atorvastatin 20 mg. Allergy: no known allergies. Family: diabetes. Personal: non-smoker, no alcohol. Triage: URGENT."
     }
    ]
